    "created_at": "2016-04-11T14:58:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-11T14:58:48Z",
    "body": "In general the spec tries to move us toward token lists for attributes that are logically token lists. Combined with PutForwards and toString() defined on token lists, this is hoped to be \"backward compatible enough\".\n\nMaybe we should give up though, if there are no implementations. It does seem doubtful anyone will want to make these changes, given that it has non-negligible back-compat risk with very little upside.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
